# IIOS Native Control

Private, dispatch-only control plane for Native Qualification v2.

Approved public source:

- repository: `mielechris/Investment-Intelligence-OS`
- commit: `@@SOURCE_COMMIT@@`
- complete inventory SHA-256: `@@SOURCE_INVENTORY_SHA256@@`

The selected-Mac job cannot start until the hosted admission job accepts the exact private repository, `refs/heads/main`, branch ref type, empty pull-request refs and `native=true`. The native job uses environment `iios-native-qualification`, exact runner labels, a detached exact-commit source checkout and a standalone inventory verifier before executing any IIOS source.

## Repository setup

1. Create private repository `mielechris/IIOS-Native-Control` with no template files.
2. Copy this candidate exactly, verify `CONTROL-FILES.json`, commit it to `main`, and prohibit tags as workflow inputs.
3. Protect `main`: require pull requests, at least one approving review, dismissal of stale approvals, conversation resolution, signed commits if available, no force pushes and no deletion. Limit bypass to the owner.
4. Create environment `iios-native-qualification`. Add the owner as required reviewer, prevent self-review when a second administrator exists, restrict deployment to `main`, and add no secrets.
5. Keep Actions permissions read-only. Permit only actions pinned in the workflow. Do not enable workflows from forks.
6. If organization runner groups are available, create an `iios-native-control` group accessible only to this private repository.

## Runner labels

Required labels are exactly `self-hosted`, `macOS`, `ARM64`, and `iios-selected-mac`. Do not add a generic organization runner group that other repositories can target.

## One-time installation checklist

1. Review the prepared archive manifest and independently compare its SHA-256 with the GitHub runner release page.
2. Extract the reviewed archive into `~/Library/IIOS/qualification/runner` only after approval. Keep the directory owner-only.
3. In the private repository, open **Settings → Actions → Runners → New self-hosted runner**, choose **macOS** and **ARM64**, and obtain the one-hour registration token only at installation time.
4. Configure the runner for `mielechris/IIOS-Native-Control`, the dedicated work directory `~/Library/IIOS/qualification/runner-work`, and label `iios-selected-mac`. Do not use `--no-default-labels` because the workflow requires the platform labels.
5. Create `~/Library/IIOS/qualification/selected-host.json` from `config/selected-host.schema.json` using the actual private repository ID, owner ID, runner name, Mac hardware UUID, current UID and pinned source binding. Seal it 0600.
6. Verify the runner appears offline until deliberately started. Use a user-level process or LaunchAgent; do not install a system LaunchDaemon.
7. Confirm `main` and the environment protections before starting the runner. Dispatch only with `native=true`, then approve the environment after reviewing the exact commit.

## Removal and revocation

1. Stop the user-level runner before changing GitHub state.
2. In private-repository **Settings → Actions → Runners**, select the runner and click **Remove**. Use the displayed removal token only with the reviewed runner removal command.
3. If normal removal is unavailable, delete the runner from GitHub first so its registration is revoked, then preserve diagnostic logs for review.
4. Move the local runner installation, work directory and `selected-host.json` into a new owner-only retired directory. Do not delete qualification evidence or rewrite historical checkpoints.
5. Revoke any unused registration/removal token by allowing its short lifetime to expire; never save tokens in files, shell history, evidence or repository settings.
6. Remove repository access from the runner group and disable the workflow if the control repository is retired.

Historical `cleanup=NOT_ESTABLISHED` remains permanent. Provider requests remain zero and all four trading authorities remain false.
